* Laser board: part models for the LTspice runs (docs/hardware/laser-board/spice)
*
* Everything here is an approximation written from datasheet typical
* values, except the laser modules, which are fitted to the sweeps
* measured on the machine. To use a maker's model instead, change the
* inside of the wrapper (OPAMP, SINKFET, CLAMPFET, RDIODE) and nothing
* else: see README.md.
*
* Parameters the netlist that includes this file must define:
*   VTS  threshold of the sink MOSFET (0.75 typical; 0.45 to 0.95)
*   VTC  threshold of the BSS138 clamps (1.3 typical; 0.8 to 1.5)

* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* Op-amp: one amplifier of an MCP6V34, simplified.
* One pole, 300 kHz gain-bandwidth, 0.15 V/us, 130 dB, output clamped
* to its rails. Its output impedance is the one in Microchip's own
* macro model (MCP6V31, rev. E): 50 ohm at low frequency, rising from
* 350 Hz to 6 kohm above 42 kHz. That model does not converge in
* LTspice, so this stands in for it. No chopping artefacts, no input
* capacitance, no output current limit, and its recovery from a rail
* is only roughly right.
* Pins as in Microchip's own model: + input, - input, V+, V-, output.
.subckt MCP6V3X_APX inp inn vdd vss out
B1 0 x I=79.6u*tanh(V(inp,inn)*1m/79.6u)
R1 x 0 3.16G
C1 x 0 530.5p
Dhi x vdd DCLAMP
Dlo vss x DCLAMP
E1 oi 0 x 0 1
Rz1 oi oz 50.6
Rz2 oz out 6k
Lz oz out 22.7m
.model DCLAMP D(Ron=1 Roff=1T Vfwd=0 epsilon=20m)
.ends MCP6V3X_APX

.subckt OPAMP inp inn vdd vss out
X1 inp inn vdd vss out MCP6V3X_APX
.ends OPAMP

* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* Sink MOSFET: PMV30UN2 (or AO3400A), as LTspice VDMOS models.
* The PMV30UN2's gate resistance and capacitances are those of
* Nexperia's own model (585 pF gate to source; gate to drain from
* 900 pF near zero volts to about 55 pF at 15 V), which the phase
* margins depend on. The AO3400A's are datasheet guesses.
.model PMV30UN2_APX VDMOS(Rg=9.5 Vto={VTS} Rd=12m Rs=9m Rb=20m Kp=14
+ lambda=0.03 Ksubthres=0.1 Cgdmax=900p Cgdmin=55p Cgs=585p Cjo=40p Is=2p)
.model AO3400A_APX VDMOS(Rg=3 Vto={VTS+0.35} Rd=10m Rs=8m Rb=15m Kp=30
+ lambda=0.03 Ksubthres=0.1 Cgdmax=400p Cgdmin=60p Cgs=600p Cjo=150p Is=3p)

* pins: drain, gate, source
.subckt SINKFET d g s
M1 d g s PMV30UN2_APX
.ends SINKFET

* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* Clamp MOSFET and Q1: BSS138.
.model BSS138_APX VDMOS(Rg=10 Vto={VTC} Rd=0.5 Rs=0.3 Rb=1 Kp=0.6
+ lambda=0.02 Ksubthres=0.1 Cgdmax=30p Cgdmin=5p Cgs=25p Cjo=20p Is=1p)

* pins: drain, gate, source
.subckt CLAMPFET d g s
M1 d g s BSS138_APX
.ends CLAMPFET

* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* Reverse diode across a module: BAT54. pins: anode, cathode
.model BAT54_APX D(Is=2.5e-7 N=1.05 Rs=2.5 Cjo=10p M=0.35 Vj=0.25
+ BV=30 Ibv=2u Tt=5n)
.subckt RDIODE a k
D1 a k BAT54_APX
.ends RDIODE

* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* A protection diode of an unpowered ESP32 pin (07_pi_off.cir).
.model DESD D(Is=1e-14 N=1 Rs=50)

* A switch for the fault runs: closed with more than 0.5 V on its control.
.model SWF SW(Ron=10m Roff=100meg Vt=0.5 Vh=0)

* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* The six laser modules, measured (bench-results, 2026-11-10 and -11):
* a diode and a series resistance fitted to each forced-current sweep
* from 1 mA to the top of its tested range. Fit error 18 and 22 mV rms
* for lasers 1 and 2, under 4 mV for the others.
*
* VALID ONLY BELOW THE POINT WHERE A MODULE'S OWN DRIVER TAKES OVER
* (lasers 3 to 6: 22.5, 22.5, 19.5 and 11.5 mA). The drivers are not
* modelled, nor whatever made lasers 1 and 2 oscillate with the
* miniSMU's voltage loop.
*
* pins: anode (+), cathode (-), opt = light in mW, as a voltage
* The capacitance across a module is unknown: the runs put it outside
* the model (Cmod, stepped), so that I(Vlas) is the diode's own current.
.subckt LASER1 a k opt
Vs a a1 0
D1 a1 k DLAS
Bopt opt 0 V=max(0, 0.275*(I(Vs)*1000-29.3))
.model DLAS D(Is=4.099e-9 N=5.333 Rs=25.85)
.ends LASER1

.subckt LASER2 a k opt
Vs a a1 0
D1 a1 k DLAS
Bopt opt 0 V=max(0, 0.130*(I(Vs)*1000-28.4))
.model DLAS D(Is=8.484e-8 N=7.652 Rs=28.70)
.ends LASER2

.subckt LASER3 a k opt
Vs a a1 0
D1 a1 k DLAS
Bopt opt 0 V=max(0, 0.347*(I(Vs)*1000-13.1))
.model DLAS D(Is=3.107e-13 N=3.294 Rs=12.20)
.ends LASER3

.subckt LASER4 a k opt
Vs a a1 0
D1 a1 k DLAS
Bopt opt 0 V=max(0, 0.555*(I(Vs)*1000-16.5))
.model DLAS D(Is=2.719e-27 N=1.292 Rs=24.30)
.ends LASER4

.subckt LASER5 a k opt
Vs a a1 0
D1 a1 k DLAS
Bopt opt 0 V=max(0, 0.140*(I(Vs)*1000-8.7))
.model DLAS D(Is=9.348e-11 N=3.711 Rs=5.95)
.ends LASER5

.subckt LASER6 a k opt
Vs a a1 0
D1 a1 k DLAS
Bopt opt 0 V=max(0, 0.565*(I(Vs)*1000-6.2))
.model DLAS D(Is=4.313e-10 N=3.963 Rs=10.20)
.ends LASER6

* The 100 ohm dummy load, with the same pins.
.subckt DUMMY100 a k opt
R1 a k 100
Vopt opt 0 0
.ends DUMMY100
